{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-27-Jun-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Two circles with centers B and D have radii DA = 8 cm and BC = x cm, respectively. AC is tangent to both circles. If DB and AC intersect the point E, AE = 12 cm and EC = 18 cm, then find the value of x (in cm).", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "Find the fourth proportion to 10, 12, and 15.", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Find the total surface area of a hemisphere with a radius of 11 cm?", "options": [{"text": "242π cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "313π cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "363π cm2", "added": false}, {"text": "273π cm2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "In an election, the winner was supported by 46% of all the voters in the list, and he got 410 votes more than his only rival. 10% of the voters on the voters’ list did not cast their votes, and 60 voters cast their ballot papers blank. How many voters were on the list?", "options": [{"text": "17500", "added": false}, {"text": "15750", "added": false}, {"text": "17445", "added": false}, {"text": "16550", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "January", "added": false}, {"text": "March", "added": false}, {"text": "June", "added": false}, {"text": "May", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "Arvind works 4 times as fast as Suresh. If Suresh can complete a work in 20 days independently, then find the number of days in which Arvind and Suresh can together finish the work.", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "What is the length of the arc of a circle whose radius is 35 cm and whose arc subtends an angle of 72° at the centre of the circle?", "options": [{"text": "38 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "56 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "44 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "28 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Study the given pie-chart and answer the question that follows. The pie-chart shows the amount of money (in ₹) spent (in degrees) on various sports by a school administration in a particular year. If ₹21,000 was spent on Football, then the money spent on Tennis and Basketball taken together is what percentage (rounded off to 2 decimal places) of money spent on Hockey and Cricket taken together?", "options": [{"text": "39.65%", "added": false}, {"text": "47.25%", "added": false}, {"text": "23.50%", "added": false}, {"text": "32.75%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "Find the value of cosecθ (1 − cosθ) (cosecθ + cotθ).", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "-1", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "The marked price of an article is 35% more than its cost price. If a discount of 15% is given, what will be the profit percentage?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "-1", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "-2", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "5544", "added": false}, {"text": "2564", "added": false}, {"text": "3590", "added": false}, {"text": "4589", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "Find the value of (13.49 + 12.51) × 13.", "options": [{"text": "438", "added": false}, {"text": "238", "added": false}, {"text": "138", "added": false}, {"text": "338", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "A merchant bought two watches for ₹9,000 each. He sold one watch at a loss of 10%. At what price (in ₹) should he sell the other watch to earn a profit of 18% overall?", "options": [{"text": "14,310", "added": false}, {"text": "14,130", "added": false}, {"text": "13,410", "added": false}, {"text": "13,140", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "The volumes of two spheres are in the ratio of 512: 3375. The ratio of their surface areas is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "If x = 3y + 4, then what is the value of (x3 - 27y3 – 36 xy) ?", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "64", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "In a class, the numbers of boys and girls are in the ratio of 3 : 5. What is the percentage of boys in the class?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "A bus covers the first 50 km of its journey in 40 minutes and covers the remaining 75 km in 40 minutes. What is the average speed (in km/h) of the bus?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1986", "added": false}, {"text": "1987", "added": false}, {"text": "1985", "added": false}, {"text": "1988", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "7823", "added": false}, {"text": "8342", "added": false}, {"text": "9000", "added": false}, {"text": "7200", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "conversion-and-melting", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "A and B can do a work in 13 days and 26 days, respectively. If they work for a day alternately, starting with A, then in how many days will the work be completed?", "options": [{"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "415 cm²", "added": false}, {"text": "154 cm²", "added": false}, {"text": "451 cm²", "added": false}, {"text": "145 cm²", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "A 255-m long train is running at a speed of 72 km/h. It crosses a platform of length 745 m in:", "options": [{"text": "50 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "53 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "51 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "40 seconds", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "train-vs-platform", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "Ashu can row 7.5 km an hour in still water. He finds that it takes four times as much time to row upstream, as it takes to row downstream. The speed of the stream is:", "options": [{"text": "2.5 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "4.5 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "3.5 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "1.5 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "still-water-and-stream-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "−1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "A mixture of750 kg of alloy of copper and tin contains 25% tin. How much tin must be added so that it becomes 70% of the mixture?", "options": [{"text": "956 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "1125 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "1097 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "895 kg", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "mixture-price", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "0.7", "added": false}, {"text": "1.3", "added": false}, {"text": "1.5", "added": false}, {"text": "2.1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "6250", "added": false}, {"text": "6270", "added": false}, {"text": "6120", "added": false}, {"text": "6050", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "Aarav owns a watch worth ₹10,000. He sells it to Bhavin at a profit of 15%. After some days, Bhavin sells it back to Aarav at 15% loss. Find the percentage profit or loss faced by Aarav.", "options": [{"text": "17.25% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "18.75% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "18.25% profit", "added": false}, {"text": "17.25% profit", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "The strength of a school increases and decreases every alternate year by 15%. If it started with an increase in 2012, then the strength of the school in the beginning of 2015, as compared to that in 2012, had (correct to two decimal places):", "options": [{"text": "Decreased by 13.85 %", "added": false}, {"text": "Increased by 12.41 %", "added": false}, {"text": "Decreased by 12.41%", "added": false}, {"text": "Increased by 13.85 %", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "The value of 30 + 180 ÷ 30 × 6 − 15 − 16 − 60 ÷ 3 − 15 is:", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "Three boys, on an average, are 25 years old, and their age are in the ratio of 3 : 5 : 7. What is the age of youngest boy?", "options": [{"text": "21 years", "added": false}, {"text": "12 years", "added": false}, {"text": "15 years", "added": false}, {"text": "24 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "ratio-of-ages", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2500", "added": false}, {"text": "4000", "added": false}, {"text": "3500", "added": false}, {"text": "3000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "Simplify the following expression: 25 × 25 + 9 × 9 + 6 × 6 + 2 × 25 × 9 + 2 × 9 × 6 + 2 × 25 × 6", "options": [{